# Individual: coho:COHO_0001881 (obsolete Hospital Universitari Vall dHebron)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0001881 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. HUVH is the Hospital Universitari Vall d'Hebron in Barcelona, Spain. Every PGS Catalog use of the id goes back to CIMBA (COHO:0000901) data: the hospital's contribution of BRCA1/2 mutation carriers, which CIMBA papers call only 'University Hospital Vall d'Hebron (HVH)' and describe no further (no study name, recruitment period or design). It is an institution label for a CIMBA site, decided as the review decided BIDMC, UPENN, MSKCC and Chicago. Do not confuse with COHO:0000564 (Heart and Vascular Health Study), which carries the acronym HVH; neither HUVH nor 'HVH' in this sense should be added there. If the curator ever mints CIMBA site samples, this would be the Vall d'Hebron CIMBA study, memberOf COHO:0000901, with PMID:32665703 as its example. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0001881 "obsolete Hospital Universitari Vall dHebron"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0001881 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

