# Individual: coho:COHO_0001917 (obsolete French National Cancer Institute)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0001917 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. INCa is the Institut national du cancer (French National Cancer Institute), France's national cancer agency, which funds, coordinates and publishes cancer data but is not itself a recruited study sample ('The pilot program IMPULSION, launched by the French National Cancer Institute (INCa)...', PMID:41820119, E542.16). The PGS Catalog lists the id among its cohorts but links it to no score or sample set, so there is no paper in which it denotes a sample; nothing names an 'INCa' cohort. Not a cohort. If the Catalog later links it to a sample, it will most likely be an INCa-funded study that should be identified by its own name. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0001917 "obsolete French National Cancer Institute"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0001917 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

