# Individual: coho:COHO_0001957 (obsolete National Institute of Health launched the Korea Biobank Array project)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 coho:COHO_0001957 coho:COHO_0000411)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0001957 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: KBA is strictly the name of a genotyping array and project; the sample it denotes is KoGES participants genotyped on it, not a separately recruited cohort. In PMID:32499647 KBA and KARE (Ansan and Ansung Study, COHO:0000530, a KoGES cohort genotyped earlier on another array) appear as separate study groups, so 'KBA' there is the KBA-genotyped part of KoGES; KoGES (COHO:0000411) is still the term it belongs to. If the curator prefers not to attach an array's name to a cohort, the alternative verdict is 'not a cohort' (a genotyping project on KoGES samples). The PGS name is a garbled fragment of the sentence 'The Korea National Institute of Health launched the Korea Biobank Array (KBA) project in 2014' (PMID:36333282). The KBA is the Korean genotyping array used on the KoGES cohorts' samples held at the National Biobank of Korea, and PMID:40778152 calls the sample 'Korean Biobank Array from the Korean Genome and Epidemiology (KoGES) Consortium (KBA)'. So the id denotes KoGES participants genotyped on the KBA: the existing aggregation KoGES (COHO:0000411). Add KBA as an acronym and the array/project names (including the catalog's name) as synonyms; obsolete placeholder COHO:0001957 in favour of COHO:0000411. Replaced by COHO:0000411 (Korean Genome and Epidemiology Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0001957 "obsolete National Institute of Health launched the Korea Biobank Array project"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0001957 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

