AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002071 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The evidence is a table row (Band et al. 2013 Table S1, https://journals.plos.org/plosgenetics/article/file?type=supplementary&id=10.1371/journal.pgen.1003509.s020, a .docx): 'Malawi | Malawi-Liverpool Wellcome Clinical Research Programme, Blantyre | University of Malawi, college of Medicine | CoM REC | Illumina 1.2M'. The PGS Catalog id has no score or sample set in the Catalog today (it is only in the Catalog's cohort table). MLWCRP is the PGS Catalog's id for the site name that Band et al. 2013 (PMID:23717212) give for their Malawi sample: the Malawi-Liverpool Wellcome Clinical Research Programme in Blantyre, the research programme that runs the Malawi severe malaria case-control study. The sample itself is the MalariaGEN partner study already in COHO as 'Human genetic determinants of severe malaria in Malawi' (COHO:0001536), which was minted from the PGS id 'Blantyre' taken from the same paper. So this placeholder is a duplicate of COHO:0001536: add MLWCRP as an acronym and the catalog name as a synonym there, and retire the placeholder (COHO:0002071). Replaced by COHO:0001536 (Human genetic determinants of severe malaria in Malawi), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002071 "obsolete Malawi-Liverpool Wellcome Clinical Research Programme, Blantyre"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002071 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

