# Individual: coho:COHO_0002233 (obsolete Groupe hospitalier Pitié-Salpêtrière Paris)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002233 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The catalog name is a mis-encoded 'Groupe hospitalier Pitié-Salpêtrière, Paris' (diacritics split in a PDF copy). Many genetic studies recruit at this hospital group (Tourette syndrome, Parkinson's disease, CJD, BRCA carriers in GEMO, and others), so without the paper the Catalog took the id from, the sample cannot be pinned down. Paris is the PGS Catalog's id for 'Groupe hospitalier Pitié-Salpêtrière Paris', a Paris hospital group (the Catalog's spelling is garbled). The Catalog lists the id in its cohort table but attaches it to no score or sample set, so there is no sample for it to denote, and no paper found by name uses a study sample so called. It is an institution name, not a cohort (the same judgement as Trinity, E1123). No COHO term matches it, and it should not be made a synonym of any French cohort in COHO. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002233 "obsolete Groupe hospitalier Pitié-Salpêtrière Paris"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002233 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

