# Individual: coho:COHO_0002273 (obsolete Prince of Wales Hospital Diabetes Registry)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 coho:COHO_0002273 coho:COHO_0001188)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002273 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The PGS Catalog id PoWHDR is not attached to any score or sample set in the Catalog's current data (REST /cohort/PoWHDR returns nothing; absent from cohort_papers.json), and Europe PMC has no paper with the exact phrase, so the PGS paper that used it could not be read; the identification rests on the name. The Prince of Wales Hospital (Shatin, the teaching hospital of the Chinese University of Hong Kong) runs one diabetes registry: the Hong Kong Diabetes Register/Registry (HKDR), 'established as a quality improvement program at the Prince of Wales Hospital since 1995' (PMID:24376643). 'Prince of Wales Hospital Diabetes Registry' is the Catalog's name for that register, which COHO already has as COHO:0001188 (whose definition already names the Prince of Wales Hospital). Add PoWHDR and the Catalog name to it; retire the placeholder. Replaced by COHO:0001188 (Hong Kong Diabetes Register), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002273 "obsolete Prince of Wales Hospital Diabetes Registry"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002273 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

