# Individual: coho:COHO_0002286 (obsolete Prostate Cancer Group, Santiago, Spain)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 coho:COHO_0002286 coho:COHO_0002284)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002286 "Obsoleted 2026-09-28. same cohort as review name E926. Same Santiago de Compostela, Spain prostate-cancer study as E926 (both PGS Catalog ids trace to the same PROGReSS entry in the same OncoArray consortium supplementary tables); see E926's note for the identity and naming caveat. Checked 2026-09-25: None: PROGReSS_PrCa is the PGS Catalog's id for the Santiago de Compostela prostate cancer study PROGReSS, the same study as E926 (PROGRESS). Both ids are recorded in papers on the prostate cancer OncoArray data, where the only PROGReSS is the hospital-based study at the Hospital Clínico Universitario de Santiago de Compostela. The Catalog's name for this id, 'Prostate Cancer Group, Santiago, Spain', is the study-group name the PGS000742 paper's table gives PROGReSS (PMID:33420416 supplement) and is kept as a synonym on E926. Same as E926; merge this placeholder (COHO:0002286) into E926's term (COHO:0002284), whose acronyms include PROGReSS_PrCa. Curated 2026-09-28: Merged into COHO:0002284 after confirming the same Spanish prostate study in the OncoArray source; both PGS ids and the source-attested study-group name are retained on the survivor. Replaced by COHO:0002284 (PROGReSS study), which now carries this term's names. Found by the checks of the placeholders' names against their sources recorded in the pipeline repository, completed 2026-09-28."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002286 "obsolete Prostate Cancer Group, Santiago, Spain"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002286 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

