AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002332 "Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The KoGES rural cohort was renamed the Cardiovascular Disease Association Study: 'the Cardiovascular disease association study (CAVAS) cohort (formerly RURAL cohort)' (PMC7670174). Replaced by COHO:0000629 (Cardiovascular Disease Association Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002332 "obsolete Rural cohort"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002332 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

# Individual: coho:COHO_0002333 (obsolete Rush University Medical Centre- Memory and Aging Project)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 coho:COHO_0002333 coho:COHO_0000810)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002333 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. RUSHMAP is not the university: in the source GWAS (Okbay et al. 2016, SSGAC well-being, depressive symptoms and neuroticism) it is the Rush Memory and Aging Project, which COHO already has as COHO:0000810. The supplement names it 'Rush University Medical Center - Memory and Aging Project' and 'Rush MAP' and thanks 'the study participants of the Rush Memory and Aging Project'. It is not ROSMAP (COHO:0000400): the Religious Orders Study is not part of this id. Add RUSHMAP as an acronym and the Catalog's and the paper's spellings as synonyms of COHO:0000810. The placeholder COHO:0002333 is then a duplicate. No COHO term carries RUSHMAP or 'Rush MAP', so there is no clash. Replaced by COHO:0000810 (Rush Memory and Aging Project), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002333 "obsolete Rush University Medical Centre- Memory and Aging Project"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002333 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

