# Individual: coho:COHO_0002382 (obsolete Sisters Study)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 coho:COHO_0002382 coho:COHO_0000660)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002382 "Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The PGS Catalog id Sisters is the NIEHS Sister Study: the ovarian cancer GWAS the id comes from (PMID:28346442) lists it as the OCAC study SIS, funded by the Sister Study's intramural grant Z01 ES044005. Replaced by COHO:0000660 (Sister Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002382 "obsolete Sisters Study"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002382 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

# Individual: coho:COHO_0002383 (obsolete St. Jude Childrens Research Hospital)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002383 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The id is used for two different St. Jude samples: ALL patients on its Total Therapy trials (source GWAS) and SJLIFE survivors (sample set PSS003603). SJCRH is the PGS Catalog's id for St. Jude Children's Research Hospital (Memphis, Tennessee) as an institution. In the source GWAS of PGS000077/PGS000788 (PMID:19684603) it denotes the children with acute lymphoblastic leukaemia treated on St. Jude's Total Therapy XIIIB and XV trial protocols. That is a clinical-trial patient series with no cohort name of its own, and the supplement expands the tag only to the hospital's name. In the evaluation sample PSS003603 (PMID:34465587) the same id denotes survivors from the St. Jude Lifetime Cohort Study, which COHO has as COHO:0001120 (SJLIFE). Because the id means the hospital and covers two unrelated samples, it is not a cohort and should not be merged into SJLIFE wholesale. The curator may still add SJCRH as an acronym of COHO:0001120, since the PGS Catalog uses it for SJLIFE in PSS003603. If so, no shared-acronym note is needed, as no other COHO term carries SJCRH. The Children's Oncology Group patients in the same GWAS are tagged COG (COHO:0000771). Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002383 "obsolete St. Jude Childrens Research Hospital"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002383 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

# Individual: coho:COHO_0002384 (obsolete Shanghai Jiao Tong University)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002384 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. The PGS Catalog's id SJTU is only the name of Shanghai Jiao Tong University; the Catalog links it to no score or sample set, and the name-search papers are unrelated. In the East Asian diabetes GWAS where the abbreviation appears, SJTU is the contributing institution, not a sample: Hwang et al. 2015 (PMID:25187374) glosses 'SJTU, Shanghai Jiao Tong University; SJTUDS, Shanghai Jiao Tong University Diabetes Study', and the AGEN-T2D supplement (PMID:22158537) lists 'SJTU SJTUDS Chinese 190 198 388 Case-control' and 'SJTU SDIID/SDS' under the institution column. The id therefore names an institution with no study sample of its own. The named sample from there is SJTUDS (E1034 in this batch); the SDIID and SDS samples are separate review names (SDIID is placeholder COHO:0002358; note that the review mapped PGS 'SDS' \"Shanghai Diabetes Study\" to COHO:0001116, the Sikh Diabetes Study, which should be checked). COHO:0000153 'Shanghai Study' (gallbladder carcinoma) is unrelated. Recommend obsoleting placeholder COHO:0002384. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002384 "obsolete Shanghai Jiao Tong University"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002384 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

