# Individual: coho:COHO_0002451 (obsolete Texas-GWA study)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 coho:COHO_0002451 coho:COHO_0000874)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002451 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. 'Texas-GWA study' is the name other groups (ICR's UK lung cancer GWAS papers) gave to the MD Anderson lung cancer GWAS of Amos et al. 2008: 1,154 ever-smoking European-ancestry lung cancer cases and 1,137 frequency-matched controls from Houston. That is exactly COHO:0000874 'MD Anderson Cancer Center lung cancer study' (definition from PMID:18385676: 1,154 cases and 1,137 controls from Houston, Texas). Add 'Texas-GWA study' as a synonym and the Catalog id 'Texas' as an acronym (no other COHO term uses 'Texas' as an acronym). Obsolete placeholder COHO:0002451 in its favour. Note COHO:0000874 already shares the acronym MDACC with COHO:0000875 (melanoma). Replaced by COHO:0000874 (MD Anderson Cancer Center lung cancer study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002451 "obsolete Texas-GWA study"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002451 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

# Individual: coho:COHO_0002452 (obsolete Twin families EBNA-1 genome-wide association study)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 coho:COHO_0002452 coho:COHO_0000744)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002452 "Obsoleted 2026-09-29. Checked 2026-09-27: The id is tied to a GWAS but not to a named cohort. 'Twin families EBNA-1 genome-wide association study' is the EBNA-1 IgG GWAS of Zhou et al. 2016 (Mult Scler, PMID:26819262), done in 'an unselected twin family cohort' by a Menzies Institute (Tasmania) and QIMR (Brisbane) team and meta-analysed with the Mexican-American family GWAS (MAFEGWAS, E658). The paper is closed (the publisher returned 403 to the download) and neither its abstract nor the two conference abstracts of the same study name the twin family cohort, so I cannot say which QIMR twin sample it is (COHO has, among others, the Brisbane Longitudinal Twin Study COHO:0000744, the Australian Twin Registry COHO:0000015 and the Australian twin-family studies COHO:0000841). Reading the methods of PMID:26819262 should settle it. TFEGWAS denotes the twin-family half of the EBNA-1 IgG GWAS of Zhou et al. 2016: 'an unselected twin family cohort' studied by a Menzies Institute (Tasmania) and Queensland Institute of Medical Research (Brisbane) team, most probably one of QIMR's existing twin studies (the Brisbane Longitudinal Twin Study, COHO:0000744, is a candidate, but only a candidate). The texts I could read never name the cohort, so I leave the id unresolved rather than attach it to a COHO term by guess; its sister id MAFEGWAS (E658) is settled as the San Antonio Family Study. Completed 2026-09-29: Duplicate of COHO:0000744 (Brisbane Longitudinal Twin Study, also Brisbane Adolescent Twin Study, BATS/BLTS). The document that could not be read before, the full text of PMID:26819262 (now cached as https://doi.org/10.1177/1352458515626598), names the analysis and its cohort: 'Queensland Institute of Medical Research (QIMR) twin families EBNA-1 genome-wide association study (QTFEGWAS)' and '3760 individuals from 1020 families in the QIMR Twin Family Cohort Study were studied'. The Catalog's name is that analysis's name, so the id is identified. For the cohort's blood collection the paper cites two references, a QIMR genome scan for naevus count in 424 twin families (PMID:17063143, abstract read: '1024 twins and siblings, plus genotypes for 690 parents', the Brisbane twin naevus families) and 'Brisbane Adolescent Twin Study: Outline of study methods and research projects' (the BATS design paper, not in PubMed and not read), and its funding section thanks 'the Brisbane twins and their families'. Its sample (twins, siblings and 1,243 parents, genotyped on the Illumina 610-Quad) is the BLTS sample as other papers describe it ('The entire BLTS sample and 1,549 of their parents have GWAS data (Illumina 610k chip)', tp.2016.36 supplement). So TFEGWAS is an analysed subset of the BLTS families, not a cohort of its own, and is merged into COHO:0000744 as its sister id MAFEGWAS was merged into the San Antonio Family Study (COHO:0000649). The umbrella term is chosen over the Brisbane Twin Nevus Study (COHO:0001550, the BLTS twin mole study that the naevus reference describes), because the paper names the cohort as a whole and cites the BATS outline as well; the curator may prefer COHO:0001550 if the families are read as the naevus study's alone. Names: carry the PGS Catalog id TFEGWAS as an acronym and add the paper's name for the cohort, 'QIMR Twin Family Cohort Study', as a synonym; do not carry the Catalog's name, which names the GWAS (as the MAFEGWAS name was not carried), nor the paper's analysis acronym QTFEGWAS. Not the Queensland Twin Registry (COHO:0001226, founded 2006) or the Australian Twin Registry (COHO:0000015): the paper points to the Brisbane adolescent twins. The Catalog uses the id in no score. Replaced by COHO:0000744 (Brisbane Longitudinal Twin Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by the checks of the placeholders' names against their sources recorded in the pipeline repository, completed 2026-09-29."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002452 "obsolete Twin families EBNA-1 genome-wide association study"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002452 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

# Individual: coho:COHO_0002453 (obsolete The Gothenburg Study)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002453 "Obsoleted 2026-09-27. The PGS Catalog id TGS (The Gothenburg Study) names two cohorts, both already in COHO: MrOS Gothenburg in the scores from PMID:40691366 (COHO:0000892) and the Gothenburg H70 Birth Cohort Studies in the scores from PMID:42237039 (COHO:0000666). It is not one cohort; the id is an acronym of both terms. Found by a check of the placeholders against the papers the PGS Catalog links to them or found by their names, 2026-09-25."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002453 "obsolete The Gothenburg Study"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002453 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

