# Individual: coho:COHO_0002470 (obsolete Trinity College Dublin)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002470 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Trinity is the PGS Catalog's id for 'Trinity College Dublin', a university. The Catalog lists the id in its cohort table but attaches it to no score or sample set, so there is no sample for it to denote, and nothing found by name is a study sample. It is an institution name, not a cohort. Samples from Trinity College Dublin that do have names are already covered elsewhere: the Trinity Student Study (COHO:0000627, which has its own PGS id TSS), the TCD/NUIG imaging sample (review row NUIG-TCD, judged not a cohort) and the MRC Genetic Resource for Alzheimer's disease site at Trinity College Dublin used by GERAD (COHO:0000646). None of these can be tied to the id Trinity, so it should not become a synonym of any of them. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002470 "obsolete Trinity College Dublin"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002470 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

