# Individual: coho:COHO_0002485 (obsolete Universita di Pisa)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 coho:COHO_0002485 coho:COHO_0002256)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002485 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. same cohort as review name E897. UDP ('Universita di Pisa') is the PGS Catalog's id for the CIMBA consortium's Pisa study of BRCA1/BRCA2 mutation carriers, which the Phelan 2017 ovarian cancer GWAS names only by its university (study code PBCS, 'Università di Pisa' in its Supplementary Table 1). The same CIMBA study appears in Barnes et al. 2020 (PMID:32665703) as 'Pisa Breast Cancer Study (PBCS)', run under the Azienda Ospedaliera Pisana ethics committee and funded by AIRC and the Tuscany Institute for Tumors ('PBCS: Italian Association of Cancer Research (AIRC) [IG 2013 N.14477] and Tuscany Institute for Tumors (ITT) grant 2014-2015-2016.', PMC7521995 supplementary files). The PGS Catalog gives that paper's sample the id PiBCS, which is review row E897 (placeholder COHO:0002256, 'Pisa Breast Cancer Study'). So UDP and PiBCS are two PGS ids for one study. Whoever curates E897 should add UDP as an acronym. 'Università di Pisa' is added as a synonym only because the GWAS's study-name column uses it; drop it if an institution name is unwanted. Do not add the acronym PBCS without an editor note: it is also the Polish Breast Cancer Study's (COHO:0000930). Replaced by COHO:0002256 (Pisa Breast Cancer Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002485 "obsolete Universita di Pisa"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002485 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

