# Individual: coho:COHO_0002523 (obsolete University of Noth Carolina Rectal Cancer Study)

AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 coho:COHO_0002523 coho:COHO_0000597)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002523 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. UNC-Rectal is the North Carolina Rectal Cancer Study. This is phase II of the North Carolina Colon Cancer Study (NCCCS-II), which COHO already has as COHO:0000597. That term's definition covers phase II: sigmoid, rectosigmoid and rectal cancer cases, May 2001 to September 2006. The two descriptions match point for point. NCCCS-II (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/research/bionlp/RESTful/pmcoa.cgi/BioC_xml/PMC3111915/unicode): \"The North Carolina Colon Cancer Study-Phase II (NCCCS-II) was a population-based case-control study of incident distal large bowel cancer (rectal, recto-sigmoid, or sigmoid cancer) in 33 counties in the central and eastern part of North Carolina.\", with cases \"identified through the rapid case ascertainment system of the North Carolina Central Cancer Registry between May 2001 and September 2006\". UNC-Rectal (E1177.17-E1177.18): the same 33-county area, the same three tumour sites, the same registry, the same dates, and controls from motor-vehicle and Medicare records. Add the catalog's name (typo 'Noth' included, as the catalog tags it) and the study's own names as synonyms, and UNC-Rectal as an acronym. PMID:26683305 also abbreviates this study as 'UNC'. That abbreviation is a paper's shorthand, not the study's acronym or a catalog tag, and COHO:0001179 already carries it, so it is not proposed. The placeholder COHO:0002523 is then a duplicate of COHO:0000597. Replaced by COHO:0000597 (North Carolina Colon Cancer Study), which now carries this term's names. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002523 "obsolete University of Noth Carolina Rectal Cancer Study"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002523 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

