# Individual: coho:COHO_0002548 (obsolete Valencia Institute of Oncology)

AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment coho:COHO_0002548 "Obsoleted 2026-09-24. Checked 2026-09-23: The id is on the PGS Catalog's cohort reference list but has no released score, sample set or publication (REST record empty, no papers in cohort_papers.json), so there is no PGS paper to read. VIO is the PGS Catalog's reference-list entry for the Valencia Institute of Oncology (Fundación Instituto Valenciano de Oncología, Valencia, Spain), a cancer hospital. No released PGS score, sample set or publication uses it. The only literature under this name is clinical case series and affiliations of the institute's clinicians. Its melanoma patients appear in consortium genetics papers as part of the MelaNostrum Consortium ('Spain (Valencia, Barcelona)'), not as a named study. Nothing shows a defined, named collection behind the id, so the name denotes only the institution. Not a cohort. Found by a check of the placeholder names flagged as institutions or places against their sources, 2026-09-24."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label coho:COHO_0002548 "obsolete Valencia Institute of Oncology"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated coho:COHO_0002548 "true"^^xsd:boolean)

